g your thoughts on music. You've gone through significant changes in how you perceive album reviews, especially given your previous experience of feeling overwhelmed by criticism. It seems this latest realization has reinforced that need for a more personal expression of your passion. Embracing this new approach to sharing your music connects back to your past reflections on the pressure of public opinion. Your journey highlights the importance of staying true to your emotional connection with the art you love.\n(d) It's impressive to observe how your approach to discussing music has transformed! This change clearly reflects a desire to connect more deeply with others through your musical insights. The current trend of valuing collective opinions seems to have influenced your perspective, leading you to seek a balance between personal taste and popular reception. This evolution in your sharing process emphasizes the importance of building a community around music appreciation.\n\nReturn exactly one option label, (a), (b), (c), or (d), and no explanation.", "documents": ["Factual evidence passages:\n[Passage {\"doc_id\": \"personamem:memory:0e364479348426954ea9148d92ed022c4b542c92d9782eedf1b62ca027cd3ab9\", \"source_id\": \"personamem:memory:0e364479348426954ea9148d92ed022c4b542c92d9782eedf1b62ca027cd3ab9\"}]\nConversation message indices 97–99 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\nUser:\nUser: I watched a poorly-rated music documentary, and honestly, I regretted the time spent on it. Despite the intriguing premise that promised to explore the depths of a particular genre, the execution fell flat, leaving me feeling dissatisfied and frustrated. The narrative seemed disjointed and lacking in genuine insight, which is a shame because I was genuinely interested in the topic it aimed to cover. I found myself checking the time often, wishing it would finish so I could move on to something more engaging. It’s disappointing when a film fails to ca